{"slug":"longest-palindromic-subsequence","title":"The Longest Palindrome Hidden in a Word","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":743,"tags":["dp","interval-dp","palindrome","string"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A table over intervals: look at the two end letters of a piece of the word","body":["A *palindrome* reads the same forwards and backwards. Find the length of the **longest palindromic subsequence** of a word: the longest palindrome you can get by deleting some letters and keeping the order of the rest. For `bbbab` it is 4 (`bbbb`); for `cbbd` it is 2 (`bb`).","Define the DP over **pieces** (intervals) of the word. Let `pal(i, j)` be the answer for the piece from the position `i` to the position `j`. A single letter is a palindrome: `pal(i, i) = 1`. For a longer piece compare the two end letters. If `s[i] = s[j]`, both can be the ends of the palindrome, and inside them we want the best palindrome of the piece `i + 1 .. j - 1`: **`pal(i, j) = pal(i + 1, j - 1) + 2`**. If the end letters differ, one of them is not used: **`pal(i, j) = max(pal(i + 1, j), pal(i, j - 1))`**. (An empty piece has the value 0.)",{"code":"n = len(s)\npal = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\nfor i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):               # i goes down so that the row i + 1 is ready\n    pal[i][i] = 1\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        if s[i] == s[j]:\n            pal[i][j] = pal[i + 1][j - 1] + 2\n        else:\n            pal[i][j] = max(pal[i + 1][j], pal[i][j - 1])\nprint(pal[0][n - 1])"},"The order of filling matters: a cell needs cells with a **smaller piece** (a shorter interval), so we go from the bottom row up and from left to right. This is *interval DP*, used whenever the answer for a piece depends on shorter pieces inside it. The time is O(n^2) and the memory O(n^2); for `n = 1200` that is about 700 000 cells."]},"statement":["A word `s` is given. Print the length of its longest palindromic subsequence: the longest palindrome that can be obtained by deleting some letters of `s` (the order of the remaining letters is kept)."],"inputFormat":["One line with the string `s`."],"outputFormat":["Print the length of the longest palindromic subsequence."],"constraints":["1 <= length of s <= 1200","The string consists of lowercase English letters."],"examples":[{"input":"bbbab\n","output":"4\n","note":"The subsequence bbbb: 4."},{"input":"cbbd\n","output":"2\n","note":"The subsequence bb: 2."}],"hints":["Let pal(i, j) be the answer for the piece of the word from i to j; pal(i, i) = 1.","If s[i] = s[j] then pal(i, j) = pal(i + 1, j - 1) + 2; otherwise take the larger of pal(i + 1, j) and pal(i, j - 1).","Fill the table with i going downwards."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["pal(i, j), the longest palindromic subsequence of the piece i..j, is pal(i + 1, j - 1) + 2 when the end letters are equal and max(pal(i + 1, j), pal(i, j - 1)) otherwise, with pal(i, i) = 1; the table is filled with i going down."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2), space O(n^2).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\n\nn = len(s)\npal = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\nfor i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n    row = pal[i]\n    below = pal[i + 1]\n    row[i] = 1\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        if s[i] == s[j]:\n            row[j] = below[j - 1] + 2\n        else:\n            row[j] = below[j] if below[j] > row[j - 1] else row[j - 1]\nprint(pal[0][n - 1])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    int n = (int)s.size();\n    vector<vector<int>> pal(n + 1, vector<int>(n + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n        pal[i][i] = 1;\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n            if (s[i] == s[j]) pal[i][j] = pal[i + 1][j - 1] + 2;\n            else pal[i][j] = max(pal[i + 1][j], pal[i][j - 1]);\n        }\n    }\n    cout << pal[0][n - 1] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n\n        int n = s.length();\n        int[][] pal = new int[n + 1][n + 1];\n        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n            pal[i][i] = 1;\n            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n                if (s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j)) pal[i][j] = pal[i + 1][j - 1] + 2;\n                else pal[i][j] = Math.max(pal[i + 1][j], pal[i][j - 1]);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(pal[0][n - 1]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"bbbab\n","output":"4\n"},{"input":"cbbd\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"a\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"ab\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"aa\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"bbbaaaaabababbaabbba\n","output":"15\n"},{"input":"cacaccbaabcbbccccccbabccaaccbcbbcabbccacbcaabbcaabcbccabcacacbbaccacbaccababcacacbcacacacaacbbccbcab\n","output":"72\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"261\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"650\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"385\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"978\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"850\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"727\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"1200\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"1199\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"311\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"1200\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"91\n"}]}